<p>Surveying the American South in the 1980s, University of Florida linguist Thomas Pyles found so many unusual personal names that he managed to make a poem of them:</p>
<p>Yerdith, Virtus, Frow, LaDonna,<br />
Nishie, Alderine, Zollie, Conna;<br />
Garalene, Methalene, Ethelyne, Fal,<br />
Bennilene, Gatsey, Ripsie, Ral.</p>
<p>Dolliree, Jetteree, Mauderie, Flem,<br />
Nubit, Wogan, Omria, Kem;<br />
Pheriba, Yuba, Twylah Jo,<br />
Ovidetta, Zava Roe.</p>
<p>Leos, Cubie, Dicie, Metha,<br />
Shi, Revonie, Sag, Uretha;<br />
Arsie, Kissie, Bussie, Missie,<br />
Yada, Telka, Clell, Elissie.</p>
<p>Ozena, Madula, Oleta, Zippie,<br />
Ozella, Schiley, Florine, Rippie;<br />
Amorus, Onan, Coeta, Pasco,<br />
Reion, Merkin, Jeline, Vasco.</p>
<p>Incia, Phenis, Phalla, Icy,<br />
Idlene, Birdene, Ala, Nicy.<br />
Rectus, Dilly, Dally, Nil;<br />
Mosco, Oco, Rumbo, Zill.</p>
<p>Stobo, Chlorine, Bamma, Floyce,<br />
Willamane, Voncile, Thair, La Voice;<br />
O&#8217;Leita, La Gita, Ludille, La Coy,<br />
Arnetta, Loonis, Fanida, Hoy.</p>
<p>Shira, Reva, Terrayne, Aslean,<br />
Etrelle, Mardelle, La Nan, Rudine.<br />
Zazzelle, Glathu, Lavora, Troy,<br />
Colonys, Wylodean, Cy, La Joy.</p>
<p>Alfa, Alto, Shyne, Arveta,<br />
Pledger, Mortis, Cance, La Nita;<br />
Anys, Cyrese, Bink, Eloyde,<br />
Verdine, Merdine, Pink, La Void.</p>
<p>Raysal, Quintelle, Raz, Zerene,<br />
Estyl, Bytha, Bevelene;<br />
Boysy, Lugen, Lavator, Lake,<br />
Eskaleen, Lueverine, Voline, Flake.</p>
<p>La Vada, La Voime, Donrue, La Nelle,<br />
Kartaleen, Avalene, Zan Jamelle;<br />
Ronalene, Darlene, Denna Fo,<br />
Japnel, Oynel, Wynell, Bo.</p>
<p>Vivett, La Carl, La Bruce, La Don,<br />
La Vondus, Burtis, Joette, Lavon;<br />
Zedro, Velpo, Bryna Lee,<br />
Zefferine, Windell, Zim, La Mee.</p>
<p>Oklahoma&#8217;s Hoyette White named her daughters Norvetta, Yerdith, Arthetta, Marlynne, and Wilbarine. &#8220;I wanted names no one had ever had and names nobody would ever want,&#8221; she said. &#8220;So I made them up.&#8221;</p>
<p>(Thomas Pyles, <a href="https://archive.org/details/namestheirvariet0000unse/page/86/mode/2up">&#8220;Bible Belt Onomastics or Some Curiosities of Anti-Pedobaptist Nomenclature,&#8221;</a> in Kelsie B. Harder, ed., <em>Names and Their Varieties</em>, 1986.)</p>
